Z||000000||loafer87gt||08-20-2001||01:39 PM||||Kinda a sad day for me. I just signed the papers at the bank and handed my Fiero over to my Dad. I know the car will have a good home as he is meticulous about his vehicles and will take care of my old ride. I will introduce him to the forum so that you guys can teach him the Fiero ropes and help him to get the car running again. It sounds kinda weird, but after three car thefts and having the car trashed, it just doesn't seem like my car anymore. The once pristine interior is a mismatch of parts from junkyards, and engine is still blown from the last incident. Someday when I'm all done school I will probably look for another GT,  for a Sunday driver car and hope I have a little better luck with it than the last. Here is a picture taken on my acreage after a fresh wax. So long old friend.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/gallery/Cars/87FieroGTsmall.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_11.jpg">      <BR><FONT SIZE="1">87 Pontiac Fiero GT<BR>72 Volkswagon Van<P>"Hard work has a future<BR>payoff.  Laziness pays off now"</FONT>||||reg||9
